# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# YC / Speedrun Launch Radar — configuration
# Copy this file to `.env`, then fill in the two tokens below.
# Everything else already works with the defaults.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── REQUIRED: Slack bot token ────────────────────────────────────────
# From your Slack app (Settings → OAuth & Permissions → Bot User OAuth Token).
# Starts with "xoxb-". See README for the 3-minute Slack app setup.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=

# The channel where alerts are posted. Use "#channel-name" or a channel ID.
# Create the channel in Slack first, and INVITE THE BOT to it (/invite @Radar).
SLACK_CHANNEL=#yc-radar

# ── REQUIRED: Apify token (covers BOTH X and LinkedIn) ────────────────
# From https://console.apify.com/ → Settings → API & Integration → Personal API token.
# The free plan's $5 monthly credit comfortably covers the default polling.
APIFY_TOKEN=

# ── OPTIONAL: polling & search tuning ───────────────────────────────
# How often to poll (seconds). 28800 = 8 hours (task default).
# POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=28800

# X search runs every 8h by default; LinkedIn every 24h (cost control —
# each LinkedIn result costs $0.005; 30 posts/poll ≈ $0.15/day max).
# X_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=28800
# LINKEDIN_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=86400

# Max items per search run (directly controls Apify cost).
# X_MAX_ITEMS=100
# LINKEDIN_MAX_ITEMS=30

# On first run, how many current listings to showcase as alerts
# (so a fresh install immediately shows what messages look like).
# COLD_START_ALERTS=3

# ── OPTIONAL: Pond integration ──────────────────────────────────────
# Set to "false" if you don't want the Pond Protocol endpoints at all.
# POND_ENABLED=true
# Access key from your Pond publishing page (joinpond.ai/agent/create).
# Only needed if you register the agent on Pond.
# POND_ACCESS_KEY=

# Database location (relative to repo root by default).
# DB_PATH=./data/radar.db
